---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About ImageLab & Open-Source Credits | ImageLab"
  description="Learn how ImageLab delivers studio-grade MozJPEG, LibWebP, PDF, and on-device AI tools completely free inside your browser with verifiable zero uploads."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 space-y-8 animate-fade-up">
    <header>
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-zinc-400 mb-2">About</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950">
        Built for Speed & Verifiable Privacy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 mt-2.5 leading-relaxed">
        ImageLab is a browser-native image and PDF studio designed so anyone can convert,
        compress, crop, redact, watermark, enhance, and manage PDFs without uploading private files to remote servers.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="studio-card rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-sm text-zinc-600 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Why Browser-First Architecture?</h2>
        <p>
          Traditional online converters upload your personal IDs, digital signatures, invoices, and
          client photos to third-party servers. By running real C++/WebAssembly encoders, local PDF
          libraries, and on-device neural models inside isolated Web Workers, ImageLab keeps
          processing instant, free, and strictly private.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Verify Zero Uploads Yourself</h2>
        <p>
          Open your browser’s <strong>DevTools → Network</strong> tab (press <code>F12</code>),
          clear the log, and process any image or PDF on ImageLab. You will see zero file upload
          requests leaving your device—our core image and PDF tools continue working even if you
          switch your browser to Offline mode after loading.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Testing & Editorial Standards</h2>
        <p>
          Every tool and technical guide published in our{' '}
          <a href="/guides" class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline">Guides hub</a> is
          tested across desktop and mobile browsers against real camera captures (JPG, PNG, WEBP,
          AVIF, and iOS HEIC) and multi-page PDF documents. We enforce magic-byte validation,
          memory-safe canvas limits, and transparent open-source licensing across the entire stack.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-zinc-950">Open-Source Credits & Licenses</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500">
          ImageLab is built on trusted open-source software. Our public frontend source code is
          available on{' '}
          <a
            href="https://github.com/thethirdclasseditor-ship-it/imagelab-free"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-blue-600 font-semibold hover:underline"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          .
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-zinc-600 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>@jsquash/jpeg (MozJPEG) & @jsquash/webp (LibWebP)</strong> — Apache-2.0 / BSD licenses</li>
          <li><strong>UPNG.js, JSZip, jsPDF, pdf-lib, exifr & heic-to</strong> — MIT licenses</li>
          <li><strong>PDF.js (pdfjs-dist) & @huggingface/transformers (Swin2SR)</strong> — Apache-2.0 license</li>
          <li>
            <strong>@imgly/background-removal</strong> — AGPL-3.0 license (complete client-side
            source code publicly available via our GitHub repository above)
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
